  "title": "South Bow Corp. (SOBO.TO): 2Q26 Recap: Gulf Coast Strength Drives Beat; Prairie Connector Execution Remains Focus",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-08-14",
  "insights": [
   "South Bow reported 2Q26 adjusted EBITDA of $280m, beating GSe of $263m and consensus of $261m, driven by strong Keystone Pipeline results and US Gulf Coast segment volumes.",
   "Management raised 2026 EBITDA guidance to $1,030m-$1,060m, though the midpoint remains below GSe of $1,055m and consensus of $1,049m.",
   "3Q26 EBITDA is guided to be ~10% below 2Q26 levels as Gulf Coast segment demand moderates.",
   "Growth capex guidance for 2026 was increased to $70m-$90m from $25m-$45m, primarily reflecting pre-FID development costs for the Prairie Connector project.",
   "The acquisition of the Liberty right-of-way from Tallgrass is a constructive step for the Prairie Connector, but permit durability remains the primary gating item for a mid-2027 FID.",
   "Management confirmed 465 kb/d of 20-year binding commitments for the Prairie Connector project.",
   "The company faces a ~$3.1b net funding requirement for the Prairie Connector, which may necessitate a financial partner to de-risk the funding picture.",
   "Pressure restrictions on the Keystone system are expected to begin lifting in a phased manner starting at the end of 2026 and into 2027.",
   "Goldman Sachs maintains a Sell rating and $32/C$45 price targets, citing valuation as a constraint to becoming more constructive."
