  "insights": [
   "PJM filed its Interim Resource Adequacy Service (IRAS) proposal with the FERC on August 13, establishing a framework for large loads (50+ MW) that do not bring their own new capacity.",
   "The proposal allows data center customers to waive curtailment compensation to fulfill ratepayer protection pledges and excludes new large load from the VRR curve to protect residential customers.",
   "While the exclusion of new large load from the VRR curve could present downside risk to capacity prices over time, Goldman Sachs does not view this as a near-term concern.",
   "The firm expects the contracting opportunity for Independent Power Producers (IPPs) to outweigh capacity price risks, helping to mitigate regulatory overhang.",
   "IPPs currently trade at an average FCF yield of 9% (10.5% excluding CEG) based on 2027 estimates.",
   "Goldman Sachs sees potential for bilateral data center contracts to start finalizing in the fall, following FERC action on IRAS by October 12 and RBP by September 29.",
